# Cursor rules for phishing-triage-assistant

You are working on a Next.js 14 (App Router) + TypeScript + Tailwind app that triages
suspicious emails with an LLM plus rule checks. Read spec.md and CLAUDE.md first.

## Code style
- TypeScript strict. No `any`. Prefer small pure functions in lib/.
- Server code in app/api and lib/. Client components only in components/ with "use client".
- Tailwind utility classes only; no extra CSS files or UI libraries.
- Validate every external input with zod (lib/schema.ts).
- User-facing text: short, plain English.

## Security (non-negotiable)
- API keys only from process.env. Never hardcode, never log, never prefix with NEXT_PUBLIC_.
- Treat pasted email as untrusted data. It goes into the user prompt inside <email> tags only.
- Never render email content with dangerouslySetInnerHTML.
- Never fetch or resolve URLs/domains extracted from an email.
- Never log email content. Log verdict, counts and timing only.
- Always defang indicators before display or copy.
- Model output must be parsed with parseModelOutput; reject anything that fails the schema.
- applyGuardrail may raise a verdict but must never lower it.

## Testing
- vitest, files in tests/*.test.ts, one per lib module.
- Mock the model with a ModelCaller function; tests must not call a real API.
- Every new rule in lib/signals.ts needs a positive and a negative test.

## Workflow
- Before finishing: npm run lint, npm run typecheck, npm test, npm run build.
- Keep commits small and focused. Update spec.md when behaviour changes.

## Do not build
- Mailbox/Graph integration, auth, database, auto-blocking, payments.
